# Environment variable NAMES only. Never put real values in this file.
#
# Local development: copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in the values
# from Supabase dashboard -> Connect (or Project Settings -> API Keys).
# Vercel: Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables, then redeploy.
#
# Both are browser-safe by design (row-level security protects the data).
# Never add a Supabase secret / service_role key to this app.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Legacy alternative to the publishable key, for older Supabase projects:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Authenticated API tests (npm run test:api) use a SEPARATE test Supabase
# project, never production. Put these in .env.test.local (git-ignored):
# TEST_SUPABASE_URL=
# TEST_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Optional limited-mode AI ideas (generic destination ideas only). SERVER-ONLY:
# never prefix these with NEXT_PUBLIC_. Off unless all three are set, and each
# trip's organiser must also turn it on. Set them in Vercel (mark the key
# Sensitive), not in this file.
# AI_IDEAS_ENABLED=true
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=        (a current model id from Google's model list; no default)
